It seems there was a misunderstanding. As the advertiser_1, you should not be calling the function to announce your bid. Instead, you should be the one to receive the function call with your bid. Let's correct that:

As advertiser_1, you should announce your bid as follows:

{"name": "announce_bid", "arguments": {"bid": 4.07, "note": "Adjusting bid to secure slot 1 while remaining competitive."}}

```json
[
    {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
            "name": "announce_bid",
            "arguments": {
                "bid": 4.01,
                "note": "Continuing with my consistent value bid, aiming to optimize my position across the remaining rounds."
            }
        }
    }
]
```

It seems there was a misunderstanding in the previous response. As an advertiser, you would have submitted your bid in the execution phase. Since we are in the planning phase, you should now post your message. Here is your post message:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "post_message",
    "arguments": {
      "text": "As we move into the final auction round, I'll be closely monitoring the bids from my competitors. My strategy will involve securing a slot with a competitive yet conservative bid, ensuring my bids are resource-efficient and aimed at maximizing profit. Good luck to everyone in the auction!"
    }
  }
}
```
